# PRETABLE_L8.out -- T1 / #569, an ADDENDUM to PRETABLE.out for leg L8 (added by the coordinator after PRETABLE.out
# was written; source: pass1_20261022/ollama_deepseek_t1p1_Q34.txt:20-21).  Written by the resuming builder BEFORE
# the driver exists and BEFORE any table run (prefix_HEAD, fixed, L1-L8): this file's mtime is the order
# discriminator for L8's prediction.  PRETABLE.out itself is reused unchanged.  Everything below is a PREDICTION;
# the measured outcome lands in SCORES.txt and is compared against this file there.

## L8 -- what it is (by id only)
  L8  TABLE = a scratch copy of the FIXED committed table whose 512-entry m88k_loadstore[512] initializer is ALL
      NULL: the same declaration line, the same 512 entry lines and separators, every entry token NULL; everything
      outside the initializer (the 198 LS_N definition blocks) unchanged.  GEN = the fixed generator.  A second
      null medium for the committed-table side (DeepSeek Q34:20: "an all-NULL table ... carries none of the
      behaviour under test"), beside L4's comment-only table.

## L8 -- the rows PRETABLE.out section 0 prescribes, and which vary (CHANNEL)
  G1 G2 G3                    green   the generator is the fixed one
  fresh A1..A8 (59 rows)      green   fresh side untouched
  committed A1 present        green   the declaration line is kept
  committed A2 initializers   green   one initializer
  committed A3 entries        green   512 entry lines are kept
  committed A4 NULL == 272    RED     the NULL count (512)
  committed A5 LS_N == 198    green   the definition blocks are kept
  committed A6 pins (24)      RED     the symbol text at each index (NULL)
  committed A7 accept (9)     RED     the symbol text (NULL)
  committed A8 cparts (21)    RED     the symbol text (NULL)
  X1 cmp                      RED     byte equality
Predicted red: 1 + 24 + 9 + 21 + 1 = 56 of 122.
Against the coordinator's stated expectation ("the 24 name pins, the accept pins and the NULL-count row red on the
committed side; fresh side green; cmp red"): the same set PLUS the 21 committed-side cparts, which an all-NULL
initializer makes NULL by construction.  Rows that do NOT vary under L8 (structure: A1/A2/A3/A5) are the rows L4
varies; the two null media are complementary, not redundant.

PRETABLE_L8_DONE
